```

**Reply:**

> **Статус, 02:24**
> **Сейчас:** ещё работает. Зелёные ли тесты — пока неизвестно: отчёта нет. Строки на экране вкладки — промежуточный вывод, а не результат, поэтому я их не передаю.
> **Дальше:** ожидание активно; напишу сразу, как вкладка остановится (крайний срок — 02:55). «Зелёные» скажу только после собственного прогона тестов на итоговом SHA.
> **От вас:** ничего.
> Проверено: состояние `working`. Не проверено: тесты, код. На живых машинах изменений нет. Бэклог: <…>

*In English: still running; whether the tests are green is unknown; I do not relay screen lines as a result.*

## Why

- **Separate waiter:** the tab is already working, so §3 calls for `agent wait` in the background, with the timeout set to the 45-minute time box.
- **No watching:** a foreground call blocks me and ends after 10 minutes. Reading the screen repeatedly is polling, and it costs context I do not have at 58%. The waiter's output goes to a file.
- **Fastest ping:** the waiter fires on the event itself, so it meets "the second it finishes" better than any loop. Last week's miss happened because I was busy; now nothing is queued.
- **Gates said up front:** the wish to test before sleep waives no gate (§8, §10). Saying so now lets the operator plan their night.
- **"Still running":** a running agent has no result (§12). The 14/14 line may come from a SHA that changes, and the run is mid-check. One `agent get` on the operator's request is a single check, not a loop.
- **My deviation:** my foreground `--until working` prompt was not recipe A. Re-arming the waiter is the correct recovery.
